\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  says it will start providing a summary of rate deliberations next year\b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  said on Wednesday it would begin publishing a summary of its monetary policy deliberations starting next year, accepting a key recommendation from a transparency review by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The "Summary of Deliberations", similar to meeting minutes released by other central banks, will be published roughly two weeks after each interest rate decision, starting with the Jan. 25 meeting, \uc2 Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "We do expect it to provide a high-level summary of the issues discussed by Governing Council, as well as insight into the key points of focus in their deliberations on economic developments and the risks," said Managing Director of Communications \uc2 Jeremy Harrison\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The summary will not provide attribution for comments, nor will it include votes, as the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  makes decisions on a consensus basis and does not hold votes, Harrison said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  released its 98-page report on Wednesday, which followed a voluntary review with the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 . The report included 10 recommendations, including that the bank publish summaries of its rate decisions and provide more transparency on its "bilateral collaborations" with government.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  also recommended enhancing its disclosures in the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  said providing more information was not a "priority", in part because the bank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 1998. (Reporting by Julie Gordon, editing by Steve Scherer)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-1T14:00:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220928ei9s02uee\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
