\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  to start releasing rate decision summaries next year\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par 17:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments, Canadian dollar)\par \par \uc2 By Julie Gordon and Steve Scherer\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  on Wednesday said it would begin publishing a summary of its monetary policy deliberations starting next year, accepting a key recommendation from a transparency review by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The "Summary of Deliberations," similar to meeting minutes released by other central banks, will be published roughly two weeks after each interest rate decision, starting with the Jan. 25 meeting, \uc2 Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "We do expect it to provide a high-level summary of the issues discussed by Governing Council, as well as insight into the key points of focus in their deliberations on economic developments and the risks," Managing Director of Communications \uc2 Jeremy Harrison\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "Given our consensus-based decision-making system, the summary won't provide attribution to individual Council members, nor will it record votes because there are no votes in our system," he added.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Canada has come under a rare attack from critics over its response to the pandemic, including misjudging inflation, which led to renewed calls for it to release minutes and be more transparent on its decision-making process.\par \par \uc2 The decision to release summaries comes as worries mount that the pace of rate increases - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lifted its policy rate by 300 basis points in six months - could lead to a recession.\par \par \uc2 Economists said providing summaries, similar to minutes released by the U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of England, could help avoid unnecessary market volatility.\par \par \uc2 "They could add valuable context on how the Governing Council came to the decision, which would fill a gap that has been evident for some time," said \uc2 Royce Mendes\uc2 , head of macro strategy at Desjardins Group.\par \par \uc2 However, much will depend on how much new information is included, added Mendes.\par \par \uc2 The bank already includes some details on its talks in the news conference opening statement at its quarterly Monetary Policy Report and in speeches after other decisions.\par \par \uc2 "Even a basic overview can be useful in correcting or clarifying potential misunderstandings. And at very least, it won't be a negative for markets," said Andrew Kelvin, chief Canada strategist at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  released its 98-page report on Wednesday, which followed a voluntary review with the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 . The report included 10 recommendations, including that the bank publish summaries of its rate decisions and provide more transparency on its "bilateral collaborations" with government.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  also recommended that the bank enhance its disclosures in the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  said providing more information was not a "priority," in part because the bank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 1998.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar was trading 0.3% higher at 1.3684 to the greenback, or 73.08 U.S. cents. (Reporting by Julie Gordon and Steve Scherer in Ottawa; Additional reporting by Fergal Smith; Editing by Jonathan Oatis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-28T16:33:25.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220928ei9s030px\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
