28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TABLE 18 - MAXIMUM CREDIT RISK EXPOSURE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par As at December 31                         2013         2012 \par (in thousands of $) \par Recognized on the Consolidated \par  Balance Sheets \par Deposits with financial institutions   $   134,544  $   414,728 \par Securities \par   Available-for-sale securities          5,257,483    5,017,104 \par   Securities designated as at fair \par    value through profit or loss          2,016,184    1,763,551 \par Loans                                   22,607,286   18,293,091 \par Off-balance sheet \par Credit commitments                     $21,646,757  $16,920,070 \par Guarantees and standby letters \par  of credit                                 355,242      374,608 \par  \par  \par MITIGATING CREDIT RISK \par  \par  In its lending \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , CCD obtains collateral if deemed \par  necessary for a client's loan facility following an assessment \par  of the client's creditworthiness. Collateral normally takes \par  the form of assets such as capital assets, receivables, \par  inventory, cash, government securities or equities. For \par  some portfolios, programs offered by organizations such \par  as CMHC are used in addition to customary collateral. As \par  at December 31, 2013, loans guaranteed by governments and \par  other public and parapublic organizations represented 10% \par  of total gross loans, compared to 13% at the end of 2012, \par  as indicated in Table 19. Policies and procedures, adapted \par  to each product, contain the requirements for appraising \par  collateral, its legal validation and follow-up. \par  \par  Where required, CCD uses mechanisms for sharing risk with \par  other financial institutions, such as loan syndication. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TABLE 19 - LOANS BY BORROWER CATEGORY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par As at December 31 \par (in millions of $ and \par  as a %)              