\par\par \b \uc2 Canada to Add U.K. Pound Assets to  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange \highlight\uc2  Account -- WSJ Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Don Curren   \par \uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 18:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Canada plans to add British-pound assets to its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve in a bid to diversify its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions beyond its current holdings of U.S. dollars, Japanese yen and euros.\par \par \uc2 The move comes after the \uc2 Canadian finance department\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  have looked at the merits of adding new \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "increase the liquidity of the portfolio and to be better positioned to respond in the unlikely event of a severe disturbance in exchange markets," the finance department said Monday.\par \par \uc2 Canada holds foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "to aid in the control and protection of the external value of the Canadian dollar and provide the Government with foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity."\par \par \uc2 Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account totaled $72.8 billion at the end of January, according to information on the finance department's web site. The bulk-- $40.4 billion--was in U.S. dollars. Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings are small compared to other major economies. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  participated in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by major central banks in 2011 to help control the appreciation of the yen, and in 2000 to support the euro.\par \par \uc2 It has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to influence the value of the Canadian dollar for many years--since August 1998.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy is to not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market except in situations where there are signs of a serious near-term market breakdown. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at The Wall Street Journal's Canada Real Time blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/canadarealtime/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/canadarealtime/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 03, 2014 12:36 ET (17:36 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140303ea33002xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
