\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  will not lose focus on inflation - Poloz\b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2013\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Poloz says can only control inflation, not exchange rate\par \par \uc2 * Hints at shift in communications, leadership style\par \par \uc2 * BoC will start holding media lockups for deputy governors' speeches\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Sept 27 (Reuters) - \uc2 Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will never shift its focus from inflation to the exchange rate, Bank of Canada Governor \uc2 Stephen Poloz\uc2  said in an interview published on Friday, confirming a hands-off approach even if the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to hurt exporters.\par \par \uc2 "You can really only control one thing," Poloz told the Globe and Mail's Report on Business magazine.\par \par \uc2 "The thing we care most about is inflation, so we're not going to ever deviate from that just because something about the dollar is bugging us."\par \par \uc2 Poloz replaced \uc2 Mark Carney\uc2  at the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  in June. His past as head of the country's export credit agency led to speculation he would be more sympathetic toward exporters' desire for a weaker Canadian dollar versus the U.S. dollar, which would help the struggling sector get back on its feet.\par \par \uc2 He has repeatedly denied any such inclination. The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate except in extraordinary circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Poloz also suggested in the interview a possible shift in the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's communications style to give a greater role to his deputies and show that policy making is not a one-man show but a team effort.\par \par \uc2 "My style is not to lead with what I think, but to sit back and let 'er go," he said.\par \par \uc2 One thing Poloz could do is allow his deputies to speak more freely in public than has been the norm. Unlike the U.S. Federal Reserve, the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's six-member governing council makes decisions by consensus rather than voting and they all stick to the same script when speaking in public.\par \par \uc2 Communicating policy decisions is largely the job of the governor through speeches and news conferences, while the deputies' speeches rarely break new ground.\par \par \uc2 But Poloz made clear any change would be incremental. He said he prefers the Canadian model to the one employed by the U.S. Federal Reserve, which has confused markets with often contradictory policymakers' views on the best strategy for rolling back from the massive bond-buying program.\par \par \uc2 "At a minimum, I would say that I wouldn't want monetary policy to be a source of uncertainty," he said.\par \par \uc2 In another sign the bank might be allowing deputies to share more of the limelight, the bank announced on Thursday it will start holding media lockups for deputies' speeches whereas until now they were reserved only for the governor's speeches.\par \par \uc2 Lockups are typically used for market-sensitive information. The system allows reporters to read the text ahead of time on the condition they don't release any news stories until a designated time.\par \par \uc2 The first such lockup will take place on a trial basis on Oct. 1 for a speech by Senior Deputy Governor \uc2 Tiff Macklem\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Starting in 2014, the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  will be in a position to hold lockups for speeches by all deputy governors, as has been requested over the years by reporters covering the Bank," said Bank of Canada spokeswoman \uc2 Dale Alexander\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CANADA-ECONOMY/BANKOFCANADA | CANT | ABN | D | M | NAT | E | U | RBN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | O | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130927e99r000dw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
