\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  not weighing C$  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  for now-Flaherty\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2012\par 17:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Says there are steps, gov't \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take\par \par \uc2 * Believes impact would be limited\par \par \uc2 * C$ hit 13-month high last week\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Randall Palmer\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Sept 17 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Canadian government\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister \uc2 Jim Flaherty\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar hit a 13-month high last week after the U.S. Federal Reserve took aggressive action to spur growth. The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise has put additional pressure on exporters already struggling with soft U.S. demand.\par \par \uc2 "There are a couple steps we could take. We have an agreement with the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  in that regard and the governor and I can take certain actions, but they're very limited in effect," he told reporters in Ottawa when asked about what options policymakers have.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he was considering using those tools at the moment, Flaherty replied "no".\par \par \uc2 In a newspaper interview published on Saturday, Flaherty said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's soaring dollar would have only limited impact because \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically reflect a country's fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Flaherty told reporters on Friday that volatility in the Canadian dollar is worrying, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength partly reflects faith in the country's economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 (With additional reporting by Claire Sibonney; Writing by Jeffrey Hodgson; Editing by Peter Galloway)\par \par \uc2 CANADA-ECONOMY/FLAHERTY (UPDATE 1) | CANT | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | FCA | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120917e89h000ze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
