\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.COM What's News - Worldwide News Briefs For Feb 3\b0\par\par\uc2 1,003 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2012\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HACKERS INTERCEPT FBI, U.K. POLICE CALL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The FBI said hackers have intercepted a sensitive conference call between the FBI and Scotland Yard cybercrime investigators.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. ENERGY MINISTER RESIGNS AMID CHARGES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. energy secretary has resigned to fight a criminal charge that he misled authorities about an alleged driving offense, forcing Prime Minister David Cameron to replace a third minister in his coalition government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ISLAMIST LEADER IN RUSSIA URGES END TO CURB ATTACKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Islamist leader who has claimed responsibility for the deadliest terrorist bombings in Russia in recent years is calling for an end to attacks on civilians now that they are protesting the 12-year-old rule of Prime Minister Vladimir Putin.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BRAZILIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  STRENGTHENS DESPITE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's real climbed against the dollar after strong U.S. jobs figures outweighed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in an attempt to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CANADA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  JOBLESS RATE RISES UNEXPECTEDLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Employers in Canada hired far fewer workers than expected in January, and the jobless rate rose unexpectedly to 7.6%, the highest level since April 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIA CUTS EUROPE GAS SUPPLIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russian natural gas supplies to Europe were curtailed as particularly cold winter weather increased Russia's domestic demand.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MEGAUPLOAD FOUNDER IS DENIED BAIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A New Zealand court denied an appeal for bail Friday by Kim Dotcom, the jailed founder of the file-sharing website Megaupload.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIGROUP HIT BY HACKING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A computer hacker group continued a wave of attacks against Brazilian financial websites, hampering the sites of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  and other prominent institutions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KHMER ROUGE JAILER GETS LIFE IN PRISON \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Khmer Rouge tribunal's supreme sourt ordered the regime's chief jailer to serve out the rest of his life in prison because of his "shocking and heinous" crimes against the Cambodian people.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. FEARS IRAN'S LINKS TO AL QAEDA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. officials say they believe Iran recently gave new freedoms to as many as five top al Qaeda operatives who have been under house arrest, and may have provided some aid to the terrorist group.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PANETTA DRAWS FIRE OVER AFGHAN SHIFT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration scrambled to clarify its plans to switch to a train-and-assist mission in Afghanistan on Thursday after NATO allies were surprised by the announcement of a U.S. strategy shift next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.N. TRIES TO STOP SYRIA VIOLENCE, AS MASSACRE IS RECALLED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Diplomats at the United Nations reached a preliminary agreement on a watered-down resolution aimed at stopping Syria's bloodshed, as the country's opposition marked the 30th anniversary of the infamous 1982 Hama massacre amid continued violence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MYANMAR SANCTIONS PUT ROCK BAND IN HARD PLACE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the volume rises inside Myanmar for the U.S. and Europe to lift strict sanctions, some noise is also coming from an unlikely quarter: a local underground rock band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU BIOFUEL DEBATE INTENSIFIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As European production of biofuels increases to comply with clean-energy laws, a tough debate has begun in the EU on whether biofuels really are better for the climate than conventional fuels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA DIPLOMACY TESTED IN KIDNAP DRAMA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China approached South Sudan to help negotiate the release of Chinese captives held by rebels in neighboring Sudan, an unusual diplomatic move that risks complicating China's ties with the two resource-rich nations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAKISTAN TO TRY PRIME MINISTER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pakistan's Supreme Court said it would begin contempt of court proceedings against Prime Minister Yousuf Raza Gilani on Feb. 13, a move which could possibly lead to the premier's removal from office.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE STRIKE KILLS 3 TERRORISTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine military said it killed three most-wanted leaders of the al Qaeda-linked terrorist groups Abu Sayyaf and Jemaah Islamiyah.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADIAN POLICE CHARGE 60 WITH CHILD-PORN OFFENSES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian police said they arrested and charged 60 men, including a day-care worker and three teenagers, for child-pornography offenses, in one of the largest such actions world-wide.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ARGENTINA BLASTS PRINCE WILLIAM FALKLANDS TOUR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With Prince William kicking off a six-week U.K. military deployment in the disputed Falkland Islands, Argentina is cranking up the pressure for talks over the status of the archipelago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ARGENTINA TAX AGENTS CONTROL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TRADING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Argentina's government this week unleashed an army of tax agents on more than 800 businesses to ensure they are following strict rules on foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH COURT AFFIRMS SCIENTOLOGY VERDICT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A French court upheld fraud convictions and fines totaling \u8364\'20\'AC600,000 ($790,000) against the Church of Scientology's Paris-based Celebrity Centre and its bookshop on Thursday, in a case highlighting the country's attempts to curtail some of the activities of the Los Angeles-based organization.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA REINFORCES ENERGY SUPPLIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina\f28 \uc2 \f2  agreed to buy a big slice of a shale-gas play in Canada from Shell, bolstering Beijing's footprint in North America's energy patch. Two other Chinese companies also sealed energy deals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOLL RISES IN COLOMBIA BOMB ATTACK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The death toll from the bomb blast outside a police station in southwest Colombia rose to 11, following a joint attack by leftist guerrillas and a drug trafficking gang working together along the Pacific coast.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY TO SEEK LIFE SENTENCE FOR GENERAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkish prosecutors said they would seek life without parole for Gen. Ilker Basbug, Turkey's top soldier until 2010 and the highest-ranking officer arrested to date in a group of court cases alleging a terrorist plot to topple the government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GROUP FORECASTS U.K. RETURN TO RECESSION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. economy will fall back into recession in the first half of 2012 and the government should implement a temporary tax cut or spending boost to stimulate demand, a leading economic research group said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. POLICE PROBE '09 EMAIL HACKING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. police are investigating, at a politician's request, a 2009 email-hacking incident at \f28 \uc2 \f2 News Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Times of London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .) [ 02-03-12 1645ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120203e823000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
