\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Dollar Surges On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Strong US jobs,  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  GDP\b0\par\par\uc2 By Satish Sarangarajan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 16:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar rallied to two-week highs against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, after six central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the greenback and stronger than forecast economic data fueled a risk rally.\par \par \uc2 Canadian third-quarter gross domestic product easily beat estimates, rising 3.5% on surging exports, while a strong private jobs data from payroll provider ADP, which came just minutes after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also raised risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 "The influx of liquidity is a welcome distraction from the troubles in Europe. Does it remove the downside risk in the euro? No. But the risk rally could last for a few days," says Kathy Lien, director, research and analysis at GFT \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar sliced through key technical support levels to hit its lowest level against the Canadian dollar in two weeks, after the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's third-quarter gross domestic product beat expectations.\par \par \uc2 The greenback plunged to C$1.0146 from C$1.0190 before the data and from C$1.0321 late Tuesday, CQG data showed. The U.S. dollar touched a day's low of C$1.0123, a level not seen since Nov. 14.\par \par \uc2 In a surprise move, the U.S. Fed, the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , the Bank of England, the Bank of Japan, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  agreed to lower the pricing on the existing temporary U.S. dollar liquidity swap arrangements by 50 basis points.\par \par \uc2 The move reduces the cost of swapping dollars in the global financial system, which has been racked by the ongoing European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The three-month euro-dollar cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basis swap, a widely watched money-market indicator of dollar funding costs, was quoted around a mid-price of minus 129 basis points, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar also drew strength from the surge in prices of crude oil, its biggest export, as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted demand for dollar denominated commodities.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, the Canadian dollar also benefited after China cut its reserve ratio by 50 basis points, a move that also lifted the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 Macro economic data from the U.S., a key driver for the Canadian dollar, also supported the risk bid, as Chicago purchasing managers index posted sharp gains in November and ADP data showed private jobs surged 206,000, significantly beating estimates.\par \par \uc2 "Here's to hoping the ADP doesn't live up to its reputation this time," said Jennifer Lee, senior economist at BMO Capital Markets, referring to ADP's history of being a sometimes-unreliable indicator of overall jobs growth. "We now look for a 125,000 gain in the headline for nonfarm payrolls."\par \par \uc2 -By Satish Sarangarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 416 306 2020; satish.sarangarajan@dowjones.com [ 11-30-11 1004ET ]\par \par \uc2 1158   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111130e7bu0003x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
