\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2011\par 12:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE INFLATION RATE STABLE IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro zone's annual inflation rate was stable at 3.0% in October, unchanged from the previous month's three-year high due to increases in energy costs, official data showed Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE CUTS GROWTH FORECAST, SIGNALING MORE STIMULUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The Bank of England Wednesday said the U.K. economy will grow more weakly than it previously expected due to the impact on exports from the euro zone's debt crisis, suggesting it may have to take further stimulus measures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ LEAVES POLICY UNCHANGED BUT DOWNGRADES VIEW OF ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided Wednesday to refrain from taking additional easing steps, but downgraded its assessment of the economy, citing a slowdown in overseas economies, and added that the yen's strength and the Thai floods will pose further risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU BARROSO, VAN ROMPUY PLEDGE TIGHTER EURO-ZONE GOVERNANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRUSSELS (Dow Jones)--European Union authorities will present new proposals for enhanced economic and budgetary governance in the coming weeks, which would strengthen the role of Brussels in overseeing national economic plans and budgets, leaders said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK OCT UNEMPLOYMENT RISES, YOUTH RATE TOPS ONE MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--U.K. unemployment rose again in October, while the number of young people without a job topped one million at the end of September, data showed Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SPAIN'S ECONOMY SLOWS, POSTS NO GROWTH IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--Spain's National Statistics Institute said Wednesday a tentative recovery in the euro zone's fourth-largest economy slowed in the third quarter, as government spending dropped due to strict austerity policies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU'S JUNCKER: AIM TO FINISH WORK ON EFSF LEVERAGE BY END NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRUSSELS(Dow Jones)--The euro zone is aiming to finish technical work on leveraging the European Financial Stability Facility, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc's sovereign rescue fund, by the end of November, Jean-Claude Juncker, president of the 17-nation euro group, said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC: TO FINE-TUNE POLICIES, KEEP PRICES STABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it would fine-tune its "prudent" monetary policy according to economic developments, aiming to maintain basic stability in price levels and strengthen prevention of systemic risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF OFFICIAL: AZUMI TOLD CANADA FIN MIN STRONG YEN POSES RISK TO JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister kept up efforts to gain international support for the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy Wednesday, telling his Canadian counterpart that the strong yen is threatening Japan's economic rebound.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY OCTOBER FINAL CPI +0.6% MM ON HIGHER VAT, ENERGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROME (Dow Jones)--Italian consumer prices rose 0.6% in October from the previous month, driven by a hike in energy prices and sales taxes, and are up 3.4% from October 2010, national statistics institute Istat said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB CONSTANCIO: ECB READY TO SUPPORT EURO-AREA BANKS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to provide euro-area banks with the liquidity they need as long as the banks offer adequate collateral in return, ECB Vice President Vitor Constancio said in an interview with Swedish daily Dagens Nyheter published Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OFFICIAL: NO GROUNDS FOR LARGE YUAN RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--There are no grounds for any significant rise in the yuan, as China's current account is becoming more balanced, a senior official at the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator wrote in an essay published Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CANADA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FIN MIN FLAHERTY: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SOMETIMES ACCEPTABLE IN EXTREME CIRCUMSTANCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Jim Flaherty on Wednesday said that market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can be acceptable in extreme circumstances.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: HK IN RISK OF RECESSION IF EURO-ZONE SITUATION WORSENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund warned Wednesday that Hong Kong may fall into recession as a worse-than expected downturn in Europe could have an outsized effect on the city, which is heavily reliant on trade and finance. [ 16-11-11 1101GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020111116e7bg0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
