ICIES, KEEP PRICES STABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it would fine-tune its "prudent" monetary policy according to economic developments, aiming to maintain basic stability in price levels and strengthen prevention of systemic risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB CONSTANCIO: ECB READY TO SUPPORT EURO-AREA BANKS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to provide euro-area banks with the liquidity they need as long as the banks offer adequate collateral in return, ECB Vice President Vitor Constancio said in an interview with Swedish daily Dagens Nyheter published Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: SPAIN'S ECONOMY SLOWS, POSTS NO GROWTH IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--Spain's National Statistics Institute said Wednesday a tentative recovery in the euro zone's fourth-largest economy slowed in the third quarter, as government spending dropped due to strict austerity policies.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CANADA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FIN MIN FLAHERTY: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SOMETIMES ACCEPTABLE IN EXTREME CIRCUMSTANCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Jim Flaherty on Wednesday said that market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can be acceptable in extreme circumstances.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: HK IN RISK OF RECESSION IF EURO-ZONE SITUATION WORSENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund warned Wednesday that Hong Kong may fall into recession as a worse-than expected downturn in Europe could have an outsized effect on the city, which is heavily reliant on trade and finance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE PREMIER: ROBUST GLOBAL ECONOMIC GROWTH IS PRIORITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vice Premier Li Keqiang said Tuesday that the world economy is currently facing sovereign-debt crises, financial shocks and a slowdown in growth, and under such circumstances, achieving robust global economic growth is the first priority.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISER: MAJOR GOVERNMENT LOOSENING UNLIKELY ANYTIME SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer inflation is likely to ease significantly in 2012 amid slowing economic growth, but the government is unlikely to loosen macroeconomic controls anytime soon, Li Daokui, an adviser to the People's Bank of China, wrote in the government-run Financial News Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT RISES 8.75% ON YEAR TO $8.3 BLN IN OCTOBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Actual foreign direct investment in China rose 8.75% in October from a year earlier, faster than in September when FDI rose 7.88% on year, data from the Ministry of Commerce showed Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA COMMERCE MINISTRY: 2011 TRADE SURPLUS TO BE AROUND $150 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's trade surplus is likely to narrow to around $150 billion this year, Chinese Commerce Ministry spokesman Shen Danyang said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA BANKS' CORE CAPITAL ADEQUACY RATIO UP AT 10.1% IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China banks' core capital adequacy ratio rose to 10.1% in the third quarter from 9.9% in the second quarter, the country's banking regulator said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SHANGHAI OFFICIAL: CHINA SHOULD SPEED UP YUAN INTERNATIONALIZATION WHEN APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's government should speed up efforts to turn the yuan into a globally used \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Shanghai's financial services chief said at a forum Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA CHANGES DEALING OPS TO ASSIST BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday detailed the make-up of a credit facility designed to help banks meet global prudential rules, outlining measures that analysts said will assist lenders adhere to the new standards.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA WAGES SLOWDOWN MAKES FURTHER RATE CUTS EASIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wages growth in Australia slowed sharply in the third quarter, sending a signal of weakness in the non-mining parts of economy and making it easier for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue cutting interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA GOVERNOR EXPECTS 4Q CURRENT-ACCOUNT DEFICIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia expects a current-account deficit in the fourth quarter as imports are likely to be higher than exports, which could reflect weakness in the Indonesian economy, BI Gov. Darmin Nasution told reporters Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA MINISTER: EUROPE NEEDS TO BE MORE PROACTIVE TO PROMOTE GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro-zone sovereign debt crisis is 'a concern' for many countries, and policy makers in the bloc need to be more proactive regarding monetary and fiscal reform and promoting economic growth, Indonesia's trade minister said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: SINGAPORE EXPORTS LIKELY FELL 8.1% ON YEAR IN OCTOBER - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's exports likely contracted for the second straight month in October, as concern over the global economic outlook reduced demand and as a high base of comparison depressed numbers further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJE(11/16) CHINA MIGHT HAVE OVER-REACHED ITSELF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are times when seemingly unrelated anecdotes are more revealing than reams of data. This just might be one of those times, when it comes to U.S. relations with China, China's economic future, and the geopolitics of Chinese economic expansion. [ 16-11-11 0906GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020111116e7bg0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
