\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2011\par 10:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ LEAVES POLICY UNCHANGED BUT DOWNGRADES VIEW OF ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided Wednesday to refrain from taking additional easing steps, but downgraded its assessment of the economy, citing a slowdown in overseas economies, and added that the yen's strength and the Thai floods will pose further risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU BARROSO, VAN ROMPUY PLEDGE TIGHTER EURO-ZONE GOVERNANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRUSSELS (Dow Jones)--European Union authorities will present new proposals for enhanced economic and budgetary governance in the coming weeks, which would strengthen the role of Brussels in overseeing national economic plans and budgets, leaders said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK OCT UNEMPLOYMENT RISES, YOUTH RATE TOPS ONE MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--U.K. unemployment rose again in October, while the number of young people without a job topped one million at the end of September, data showed Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SPAIN'S ECONOMY SLOWS, POSTS NO GROWTH IN 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--Spain's National Statistics Institute said Wednesday a tentative recovery in the euro zone's fourth-largest economy slowed in the third quarter, as government spending dropped due to strict austerity policies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU'S JUNCKER: AIM TO FINISH WORK ON EFSF LEVERAGE BY END NOVEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRUSSELS(Dow Jones)--The euro zone is aiming to finish technical work on leveraging the European Financial Stability Facility, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc's sovereign rescue fund, by the end of November, Jean-Claude Juncker, president of the 17-nation euro group, said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC: TO FINE-TUNE POLICIES, KEEP PRICES STABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it would fine-tune its "prudent" monetary policy according to economic developments, aiming to maintain basic stability in price levels and strengthen prevention of systemic risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF OFFICIAL: AZUMI TOLD CANADA FIN MIN STRONG YEN POSES RISK TO JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister kept up efforts to gain international support for the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy Wednesday, telling his Canadian counterpart that the strong yen is threatening Japan's economic rebound.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY OCTOBER FINAL CPI +0.6% MM ON HIGHER VAT, ENERGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROME (Dow Jones)--Italian consumer prices rose 0.6% in October from the previous month, driven by a hike in energy prices and sales taxes, and are up 3.4% from October 2010, national statistics institute Istat said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB CONSTANCIO: ECB READY TO SUPPORT EURO-AREA BANKS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 STOCKHOLM (Dow Jones)--The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to provide euro-area banks with the liquidity they need as long as the banks offer adequate collateral in return, ECB Vice President Vitor Constancio said in an interview with Swedish daily Dagens Nyheter published Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OFFICIAL: NO GROUNDS FOR LARGE YUAN RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--There are no grounds for any significant rise in the yuan, as China's current account is becoming more balanced, a senior official at the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator wrote in an essay published Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CANADA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FIN MIN FLAHERTY: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SOMETIMES ACCEPTABLE IN EXTREME CIRCUMSTANCES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Jim Flaherty on Wednesday said that market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can be acceptable in extreme circumstances.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: HK IN RISK OF RECESSION IF EURO-ZONE SITUATION WORSENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund warned Wednesday that Hong Kong may fall into recession as a worse-than expected downturn in Europe could have an outsized effect on the city, which is heavily reliant on trade and finance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE PREMIER: ROBUST GLOBAL ECONOMIC GROWTH IS PRIORITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vice Premier Li Keqiang said Tuesday that the world economy is currently facing sovereign-debt crises, financial shocks and a slowdown in growth, and under such circumstances, achieving robust global economic growth is the first priority.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISER: MAJOR GOVERNMENT LOOSENING UNLIKELY ANYTIME SOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer inflation is likely to ease significantly in 2012 amid slowing economic growth, but the government is unlikely to loosen macroeconomic controls anytime soon, Li Daokui, an adviser to the People's Bank of China, wrote in the government-run Financial News Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE EXPORTS LIKELY FELL 8.1% ON YEAR IN OCTOBER - POLL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's exports likely contracted for the second straight month in October, as concern over the global economic outlook reduced demand and as a high base of comparison depressed numbers further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJE(11/16) CHINA MIGHT HAVE OVER-REACHED ITSELF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are times when seemingly unrelated anecdotes are more revealing than reams of data. This just might be one of those times, when it comes to U.S. relations with China, China's economic future, and the geopolitics of Chinese economic expansion. [ 11-16-11 0455ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020111116e7bg0001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
