\par\par \b \uc2 Harper says \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  can act on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 :Bloomberg\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2011\par 23:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Sept 21 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a speculative appreciation of the Canadian dollar, Prime Minister Stephen Harper said in an interview published on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News quoted Harper as saying that the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  would not tolerate an appreciation in the Canadian dollar if it undermined the Canadian economy.\par \par \uc2 Monetary authorities "would be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they thought there were movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that were contrary to the country's interests and not being driven by actual underlying fundamentals," Bloomberg quoted Harper as saying.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's web site outlines strict guidelines on when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and says the bank does not target a specific level for the Canadian dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to affect the Canadian dollar since September, 1998.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on a discretionary, rather than a systematic, basis and only in exceptional circumstances," the bank says, citing market breakdown, extreme price volatility, liquidity crunches or extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements as possible reasons.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  is fiercely independent and it is rare for politicians to comment on monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Even as Harper spoke, the Canadian dollar was weakening not strengthening, sinking to its weakest level since December on concerns about the outlook for the U.S. economy. [CAD/]\par \par \uc2 The full policy is available here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bankofcanada.ca/about/backgrounders/intervention-foreign-exchange-market/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bankofcanada.ca/about/backgrounders/\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight22 -market/}}}\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Janet Guttsman; Editing by Jeffrey Hodgson)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CANADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110924e79l000ms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
