\par\par \b \uc2 AT A GLANCE: Fukushima Nuclear Accident Ranked Alongside Three Mile Island\b0\par\par\uc2 1,475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    THE NEWS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The nuclear accident at the Fukushima plant now ranks alongside Three Mile Island in terms of seriousness on an international nuclear accident scale, Japan's nuclear safety agency said Friday. The agency raised the accident rating to level five from four after considering the suspected extent of damage to fuel at the plant's reactors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Japanese Self Defense Force finished its water cooling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  using water cannons and fire trucks. Seven trucks trained water on Reactor No. 3, which is thought to present the greatest immediate danger. An SDF official said radiation levels were low enough not to present a health risk to SDF members conducting the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped massive quantities of yen Friday, aiming to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record surge from further damaging an economy ravaged by earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disaster.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    NUCLEAR PLANT STATUS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Naoto Kan pledged to disclose as much information as possible on the ongoing nuclear crisis to the international community during his meeting Friday with International Atomic Energy Agency Chief Yukiya Amano and said an agency team will be dispatched "within a couple of days" to monitor radiation levels in Tokyo, as well as near the quake-hit plant.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Yukio Edano said progress was being made to reconnect power at the stricken plant. Restoring electricity to the reactor's cooling systems could represent the major breakthrough needed for bringing the crisis at the plant under control. A nuclear safety agency official said Reactors No. 1 and No. 2 would be reconnected first, within the day, while Reactor No. 3 wouldn't get power until as late as Sunday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government official reiterated that cooling Reactor No. 3 remained the main priority, since it is believed that spent fuel in a tank at the reactor is exposed, presenting a high radiation risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Evacuation Area\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Radius of 20 kilometers; those between 20 kilometers and 30 kilometers of the plant told to stay indoors.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped massive quantities of yen Friday, aiming to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's record surge from further damaging the country's economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In an extraordinary trading session in Europe, several European central banks were seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a bid to tame the sky-high yen. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Bundesbank, the Bank of France, the Bank of England and later the Bank of Italy came after the Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight, spending around Y1 trillion to Y2 trillion buying dollars against the yen. The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also confirmed that it had participated in selling the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires' coverage of the event and related news can be found by searching the code R/JA.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LATEST STORIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NUCLEAR DEVELOPMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN NUCLEAR AGENCY: FUKUSHIMA HIKED TO SAME ACCIDENT LEVEL AS THREE MILE ISLAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japan Nuclear and Industrial Safety Agency said Friday it raised the accident scale level of the quake-damaged Fukushima Daiichi nuclear-power complex to 5, similar to the level of the accident at Three Mile Island in 1979. (published 0919 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IAEA CHIEF SAYS JAPAN NUKE PLANT CRISIS 'A RACE AGAINST TIME' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.N. International Atomic Energy Agency chief Yukiya Amano said Friday that Japan's battle to stabilize a crippled nuclear plant was "a race against time." (published 0936 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: TOKYO RADIATION TAD HIGHER THAN NORMAL, STILL NEGLIGIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Radiation levels in the Tokyo area were around typical background levels on Friday afternoon, while in areas close to the quake-damaged Fukushima nuclear power plant they remained high but still below levels that would pose a threat to human health, officials said. (published 1305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SELF DEFENSE FORCE: RADIATION LEVELS LOW ENOUGH TO ENSURE SDF MEMBERS' SAFETY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A top official at Japan's Self Defense Force said Friday that radiation levels at the earthquake-damaged Fukushima Daiichi nuclear-power complex are low enough to ensure the safety of the members at the scene. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FRENCH NUCLEAR AGENCY: THE SITUATION IN JAPAN REMAINS SERIOUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The situation at the stricken Fukushima nuclear power plant in Japan remains serious, with radiation still being emitted into the atmosphere, and the situation could worsen, a senior French nuclear safety official said Friday. (published 1015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IAEA CHIEF: AGENCY TEAM TO MONITOR RADIATION NEAR NUCLEAR PLANT - KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 International Atomic Energy Agency Chief Yukiya Amano said Friday that an IAEA team will be dispatched "within a couple of days" to near the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant to monitor radiation there, Kyodo News reported. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 /MARKETS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; BUYS DOLLARS, SELLS YEN IN NEW YORK TRADING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday, buying dollars and selling yen as part of a coordinated effort by Group of Seven nations to weaken Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 1255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THREE US BANKS SAY FED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TOTALED $50 MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Federal Reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Friday morning to stem yen strength in the amount of $50 million, according to three U.S. banks familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 1337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BANK OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CANADA INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , BUYS CANADIAN DOLLARS VERSUS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Friday morning as it joined the international effort to quell strength in the yen. (published 1249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TAMES YEN, BUT LITTLE FURTHER WEAKNESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen edged higher in London trading hours, despite European central banks stepping in to sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of coordinated action by the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations to stabilize the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after its recent record surge. (published 1149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 5TH UPDATE: G-7 PLEDGES RARE JOINT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS CRISIS-STRICKEN JAPAN SELLS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped massive quantities of yen Friday, aiming to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's record surge from further damaging an economy ravaged by earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disaster. (published 0739 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ OFFERS Y3 TLN SAME-DAY FUNDS TO EASE QUAKE FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan offered to inject another Y3 trillion in same-day funding Friday morning to calm jitters in the markets due to the massive earthquake and subsequent nuclear power crisis, marking a fifth straight day of the bank's emergency action. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHRS END MOSTLY UP; TOKYO LEADS GAINS AS YEN DROPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo led most Asian markets higher Friday after some of the world's largest economies agreed to put their weight behind Japan's effort to interrupt the yen's surge. (published 1037 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ 4TH UPDATE: JAPAN FACES MISTRUST AS NUCLEAR EFFORTS CONTINUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. government, signaling distrust of reports from Japan about the nuclear crisis there, moved Thursday to evacuate U.S. citizens and set up its own channels of information--a step echoed by some American companies that laid plans to trim their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the stricken country. (published 1157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOST JAPANESE AIRPORTS HAVE FUEL SUPPLIES FOR 10 DAYS - IATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Airlines Friday were urged to use fuel supplies in Japan efficiently as stocks at some airports fell to 10 days' worth of supply. (published 1142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par COLD WEATHER TO LINGER IN JAPAN; WINDS LIKELY OFFSHORE IN FUKUSHIMA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A spell of cold weather will likely continue in earthquake- and tsunami-affected areas of Japan, slowing down rescue efforts, weather agencies said Friday. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA PRIME MINISTER: JAPAN EVENTS TO PROMPT US TO REVISIT SAFETY STRATEGIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mounting concerns over damaged nuclear reactors in Japan will prompt India to revisit its own nuclear safety strategies, Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh said Friday, indicating the island nation's trauma will play a significant role in shaping the final framework for handling nuclear accident liabilities in India. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SONY: 6 MANUFACTURING PLANTS IN JAPAN HAVEN'T RESUMED PRODUCTION AS OF FRIDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday six of its manufacturing plants that make various devices and components, including Blu-ray discs and lithium-ion batteries, remain closed following the massive earthquake and tsunami that struck the country last week. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2nd UPDATE: Honda Suspends Japan Auto, Motorcycle Assembly Through Wed; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mazda\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Mitsubishi Resume Some Production \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Honda Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (7267.TO) said Friday that it will continue to suspend automobile and motorcycle assembly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through Wednesday, as some of its suppliers need more time to restore their production facilities damaged by the devastating quake off northeast Japan a week ago. (published 1255 GMT) [ 18-03-11 1359GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0013i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
