\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK: Libya Ceasefire Calms Oil Market, For Now\b0\par\par\uc2 1,215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 9:05 (Dow Jones) Nymex crude futures tumble nearly $3 from recent levels to $100.38/barrel after a ceasefire is declared by Libya's foreign minister. The threat of air strikes by Western powers led to the halt by pro-regime forces. Crude traders were fearful of escalation should foreign powers enter the fight, but any signs of calmed tensions between opposition forces and Gadhafi's regime is a step, however small, towards getting Libyan oil supplies flowing again. Of course, official reports from Libyan officials have many doubters. More concrete signs likely needed before oil markets relax. (jerry.dicolo@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:05 (Dow Jones) Banks, and investors, anxiously await stress-test results today, a tip-off that should separate the strong from the weak. Now Fifth Third (FITB) is gaining consensus as a Cinderella pick to advance with the blue chips. Last month FITB still owed Uncle Sam $3.4B TARP funds. Just Tuesday it repurchased Treasury's warrants. Two weeks ago it disclosed an SEC probe. Most thought it a Morehead State with little chance to knock off a powerhouse. But KBW today upgrades FITB to outperform saying most don't expect the dividend boost, but it does now. FITB up 3.1% premarket to $14.24. (david.benoit@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:02 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  (SBUX) said earlier this month it wasn't considering raising prices on its coffee, but will the scarcity of beans and price increases by its rivals pressure it to have a change of heart? Kraft (KFT) announced Wednesday it has raised US prices 20% per pound equivalent for its ground Yuban and Maxwell House brands as arabica coffee prices are up nearly 45% the past six months. Smucker (SJM) lifted prices 10% for most of its coffee last month. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is forging plans to increase its presence in the packaged retail coffee market, and price adjustments may be to come. (leslie.josephs@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:58 (Dow Jones) Gold prices slip from session highs after Libya's foreign minister declares an immediate ceasefire. The precious metal is considered a safe haven from political uncertainty, and prices tend to ease when crises stabilize. Comex April gold recently up 1% at $1,417.60/troy ounce. (tatyana.shumsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:54 (Dow Jones) Lorillard (LO) shares bouncing around this morning after FDA panel says in draft report it won't recommend an outright ban on menthol. LO first up more than 6%, now off 10% to $71.11. FDA isn't required to follow the committee's advice, but analysts had been concerned the group would at least try to get menthol cigarettes off the shelves. LO derives the vast majority of its revenue from menthol products. \uc2 Reynolds American\uc2  (RAI) and \uc2 Altria\uc2  (MO) also fall into the red after early pop. (melissa.korn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:50 (Dow Jones) Details are light on yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but all indications are that the initial bout of yen buying was modest. Most market players are refusing to comment on the size of orders, but consensus appears to be "modest". That may indicate that G7 officials are looking to keep their powder dry and jump back into the market later in the day. Around the time the stock market opens could be an ideal time. The buzzword amongst market participants is "stability"--G7 authorities are aiming to dissuade any more aggressive moves (some analysts see Y80 as the line in the sand for dollar/yen, though official bids are said to lie in wait around Y81). USD/JPY around Y81.53 after spiking near Y82 at 8 a.m. EDT. (javier.david@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:45 (Dow Jones) S&P raised its issuer credit rating on Villanova University to A+ from A. Villanova is scheduled to play George Mason in the NCAA basketball tourney this afternoon so even if the PA team loses today, "at least they have the consolation price of an S&P ratings upgrade," wrote one analyst. Strong demand and financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were cited by S&P as factors behind the upgrade. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:44 (Dow Jones) Encana's (ECA) purchase of a 30% interest in the Kitimat LNG project in Canada's west coast increases the chances that the first major initiative to export North American gas will move forward--and soon, says Tudor Pickering Holt. The research firm notes a final investment decision is likely to come in late 2011, with the last hurdle being getting long-term gas prices indexed on oil. Shares up fractionally premarket amid a broader market rise. (angel.gonzalez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:37 (Dow Jones) Canadian dollar falls back after 8 a.m. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help push the yen lower. "I'm guessing that it's not as big as people had anticipated," says C.J. Gavsie, managing director of corporate and institutional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at BMO Capital Markets. He estimates that the tally likely was in the tens, not hundreds, of millions. The Canadian dollar was at Y82.79 recently, according to CQG. That's down from at Y83.33 at 8 a.m. EDT, at the time of the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:27 (Dow Jones) Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was nominal, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could re-enter later in the day, says Michael Woolfolk, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon in New York. He calls the initial move symbolic to show the Fed stood with the Bank of Japan, but that it was also a "warning shot across the bow" of speculators trying to fight the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar is at about Y81.37 in Friday morning trading in New York from around Y79 late Thursday. (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:12 (Dow Jones) One day after Colombia President Juan Manuel Santos hinted Canada-based Greystar's (GSL.T) Angostura open-pit gold mine project was unlikely to be granted environmental approval, the company late Thursday gave up trying. "What happens next?" asks Chile-based Celfin Capital. "It's a case of rip it up and start again, one imagines, with an underground project now needing to be designed. And it could well be that they need a partner to help them pick up the slack given the massive investment they have already made." (dan.molinski@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:01 (Dow Jones) The G7's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's strength hurt Treasurys overnight while stocks rallied, but tensions in Libya and uncertainty about Japan's nuclear crisis bring buyers back to safe-haven bonds. Some traders also say Treasurys could benefit as Japan need to recycle their dollar proceeds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds, especially short to intermediate maturities, tend to be the parking slot. The 10-year note is 1/32 higher, yielding 3.251%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Equities Market Talk Editors, \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Paul Vigna, 212 416-2184,paul.vigna@dowjones.com \par Visit the Market Talk website at  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 18, 2011 09:05 ET (13:05 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110318e73i0034s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*