 and finance ministry do have measures available to tackle any sudden "irregularities" in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Market are markets. They will find their own level for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said in an interview on the sidelines of the World Economic Forum's annual meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian policymakers won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in the way that some Latin American countries have done, he said. Countries like Brazil have put in types of capital control, while Chile recently announced a big \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Flaherty said: "There are some measures that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  can take with the minister of finance that would be temporary short term things we could do. We would only do that if there is some irregularity in the market, sudden appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --dramatic things like that."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said that Canadian policymakers don't have any such measures planned. "We are not planning to do anything like that," he said. "This is a market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and it will remain a market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 28, 2011 06:05 ET (11:05 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110128e71s0022e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscale