\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Canada Finance Minister: Markets Will Find Level For  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2011\par 12:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Anjali Cordeiro \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 DAVOS, Switzerland (Dow Jones)-Canada will continue to let market forces determine the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister James Flaherty said Friday, but noted that both the ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have measures available to tackle any sudden "irregularities" in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 "Market are markets. They will find their own level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Flaherty said in an interview on the sidelines of the World Economic Forum.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar has been gaining against the greenback, hurting Canadian exporters. Some countries in similar straits, including Brazil and Chile, have introduced capital controls and/or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on foreign exchanges, but Flaherty said \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't follow their example,\par \par \uc2 Still, he said there are some "temporary short-terms measures" that the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  can take with the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We would only do that if there is some irregularity in the market, sudden appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --dramatic things like that," he said.\par \par \uc2 Right now, no such measures are planned, he said.\par \par \uc2 "Other than that, this is a market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and it will remain a market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The rising cost of food and fuel have contributed to the stronger Canadian dollar.\par \par \uc2 Canada is encouraging other countries like China to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  be more flexible, Flaherty said.\par \par \uc2 China's tight grip on its exchange rate "creates distortions and contributes to imbalances in the world," he said. "In a world where we are all seeking to have free trade, part of [the] responsibility is to make sure that your \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is part of the open market."\par \par \uc2 Canada isn't going to have "fantastic" economic growth this year, he said, predicting moderate growth of 2% to 3% this year and next year.\par \par \uc2 -Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200; anjali.cordeiro@dowjones.com [ 28-01-11 1159GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110128e71s0014d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
