\par\par \b \uc2 DJ 2nd UPDATE: Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2 's Carney:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Would Be Joint Move\b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2010\par 05:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds further comments from Carney on the U.S. Fed's plans, avoiding deflation; adds details.)\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA -(Dow Jones)- \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Mark Carney said Wednesday unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market 'seldom works.'\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would do so in cooperation with other countries, Carney said in testimony to the Senate banking committee.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank and the federal government would contemplate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two scenarios. One is if there was a 'disruption' in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, which he said was relatively rare.\par \par \uc2 The second situation, he said, is if 'extreme movements' in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market 'seriously imperiled conditions that would support sustainable long-term growth.'\par \par \uc2 'Unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without backing policy actions seldom works sustainably,' Carney said. 'If conditions warranted, we would look to act with our partners in advanced economies and emerging economies if necessary. And we would always work to ensure that underlying policy was consistent with the action.'\par \par \uc2 Carney said the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's economic forecasts assume additional monetary stimulus by the U.S. Federal Reserve. He said it was 'no secret' that the Fed is discussing additional quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 'The point is obviously to avoid further disinflation and deflation, and given the debt dynamics in the United States, not just at the government level but very importantly at the personal level, it would be unhelpful to move into a deflationary environment,' he said. 'That's a downside risk obviously for the Canadian economy and it's one we watch closely.\par \par \uc2 Carney also said there's a need to remain 'vigilant' on household debt in Canada. -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 613-237-0668; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020101028e6as003s6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
