\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Unilateral  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  rarely effective: BOC\b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2010\par 00:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * BoC would prefer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with others - Carney\par \par \uc2 * Carney gives no indication bank ready to act now\par \par \uc2 * Says rates abnormally low, must be vigilant on debt (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Louise Egan\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is rarely effective and if the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  wanted to act, it would look to do so with other countries, Governor Mark Carney said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Carney noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-established policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in cases of disruption in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or when extreme movements in the value of the Canadian dollar threatened the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without backing policy actions seldom works sustainably. If conditions warranted we would look to act with our partners in advanced economies and emerging economies if necessary," he told the Canadian Senate's banking committee.\par \par \uc2 "We would always work to ensure that underlying policy was consistent with the action," he said.\par \par \uc2 Carney did not suggest such action was imminent. The last time the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to influence the level of the Canadian dollar was in 1998.\par \par \uc2 Many major world economies, shaken by three years of financial turmoil, have recently taken steps to cap or weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a fight over fragile global demand for exports. These include Japan and Brazil. China also faces widespread calls to let the yuan appreciate more quickly.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar <CAD=D4> briefly shot past parity with the U.S. dollar earlier this month, putting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength firmly back on the bank's radar amid signs the export-reliant economy's recovery is losing steam.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated on Wednesday as the greenback rose broadly on speculation the U.S. Federal Reserve would take a measured approach to adding further stimulus through asset purchases, or quantitative easing. [CAD/]\par \par \uc2 Carney, who has openly fretted about high levels of household debt in Canada, once again reminded Canadians that interest rates are "abnormally low" and that individuals should ensure their debt load will be sustainable when rates inevitably rise.\par \par \uc2 "Our role is limited. At this stage our role is principally to identify the issue rigorously," he said.\par \par \uc2 "There is an element of ... identification of the issue to the public, to ask people to be aware, to remind people that we're living in abnormal times."\par \par \uc2 He also said authorities must be vigilant about the possibility of a build of up of excessive debt as a result of keeping interest rates low for an extended period of time.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark overnight target rate unchanged last week at 1 percent, following three successive hikes between June and September. Markets do not expect the bank to raise rates again until well into 2011. (Additional reporting by Ka Yan Ng and David Ljunggren; Editing by Jeffrey Hodgson)\par \par \uc2 CANADA-ECONOMY/BANKOFCANADA (PIX, UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|CANT|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101027e6ar001u7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
