\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  says  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  concerns on G7 meeting agenda\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 17:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , flexibility to be on G7 agenda\par \par \uc2 * Flaherty says Geithner "has a point" on IMF reform, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Ottawa will bring strong stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to table\par \par \uc2 By John McCrank\par \par \uc2 OTTAWA, Oct 6 (Reuters) - Concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and inflexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes will be on the agenda at the upcoming meeting of \uc2 Group\uc2  of Seven policymakers, Canadian Finance Minister Jim Flaherty said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "There are concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. There are concerns about inflexibility, relatively speaking, of certain \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world. This is a topic that I'm sure we will be discussing," he told reporters in Ottawa.\par \par \uc2 Group\uc2  of Seven finance ministers and central bankers will gather informally on Friday ahead of the International Monetary Fund's twice-yearly meetings in Washington this weekend. Finance chiefs from the main global economic forum, the G20 emerging and industrialized nations, are scheduled to meet on Oct. 22 in South Korea.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions have risen to the top of the agenda for these meetings as policy makers deal with a drive by many of the world's economies to cap the strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In pointed remarks earlier on Wednesday, U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner said that the problem of undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some emerging economies was "inherently a multilateral problem" that would take a cooperative effort to solve in the form of an effective multilateral mechanism to push countries with big current account surpluses to abandon export-oriented policies. [ID:nN06208024]\par \par \uc2 He suggested the IMF should have more capacity to "make a difference" in these issues. IMF member countries are negotiating governance reforms that would give emerging economies more clout in the organization.\par \par \uc2 "It's worthwhile making sure those reforms to governance, which we deeply believe in and support, are complemented by more effective ways for the IMF to play a greater role in helping change behavior on the exchange rate front and encourage surplus countries to shift to more domestic demand led growth," Geithner said.\par \par \uc2 "That's the basic deal on offer," he added.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Geithner's comments on IMF reform and exchange rate policy, Flaherty said Geithner "has a point."\par \par \uc2 "He and I have had discussions of late on that and other subjects," he said.\par \par \uc2 China's reluctance to let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate more quickly has prompted stronger rhetoric from the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 A senior Canadian finance official said on Wednesday that Ottawa would bring to the multilateral table a strong stance in favor of flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he declined to comment on the nature of any possible negotiations for an agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 Flaherty urged against a "distortions in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values or distortions in trading relationships."\par \par \uc2 "There is a danger here that countries that do have \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that trade in a market, that trade freely, are disadvantaged by certain \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are made by other countries and by inflexibility of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. (Additional reporting by Louise Egan; editing by Jeffrey Hodgson)\par \par \uc2 G7-CANADA/FLAHERTY (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|CANT|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101006e6a60016h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
