\par\par \b \uc2 BOC: Declines To Comment On Japanese  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Karen Johnson   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 17:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that has pushed the dollar and euro sharply higher against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Jill Vardy, acting chief of communications for the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 , said \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have no comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen was falling steeply Wednesday after Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in more than six years.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities said they are prepared to extend the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the North American session and possibly into Thursday, according to a Kyodo news report.\par \par \uc2 After the U.S. dollar fell to a 15-year low Tuesday of Y82.87, the initial barrage of yen-selling orders hit the market early in the Asian day; it was followed by bursts that pushed the dollar above Y85. The dollar was at Y85.63 in late morning in New York on Wednesday, from Y83.08 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 The Canadian dollar was at Y83.49, from Y81.12 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  about 20 minutes after the first sales hit the marke