ation in core inflation and Capital Economics says the bond market is right to be relatively sanguine over the outlook. "We see scope for 10-year gilt yields both to ease down further to around 2.75%." September gilts up 0.29 at 125.02, having hit a 125.23 contract high. 10-year gilt at 114.639 yielding 2.975%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1415 GMT [Dow Jones] USD broadly stronger, with ICE Dollar Index notching one-month high at 83.200 from 82.347 late Thu, according to EBS via CQG. EUR/USD recently hit intraday low at 1.2673 from 1.2820, as dovish ECB comments and downgrade of France's 2011 growth prospects combine with recent stream of weakening US data, leading investors to flee riskier assets. DJIA down nearly 1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (bradley.davis@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1404 GMT [Dow Jones] Week's deals have been generally well accepted in muni mkt, thanks to continued light supply and strong demand. "Munis have had a nice run, following the Treasury market," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eaton Vance\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Evan Rourke. Fri, munis holding firm, with prices little changed and low trading volume, he says. Looking ahead, it's another light issuance week, with $533M deal from South Calif Public Power one of largest offerings, according to Ipreo. Market participants expect supply to pick up sometime after Labor Day.(kelly.nolan@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1402 GMT [Dow Jones] The index rose earlier to 83.214, which the current high for the uptrend from the Aug. 6 low of 80.085. See chart at\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4462"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4462}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 The index is closing in on target resistance at 83.385. But a move below 82.935 would instead point it down to 82.347.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (stephen.cox@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1353 GMT [Dow Jones] Russia is less likely t